      "prompt": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is <Picture 1> Pixel Dusk from the first character reference sheet: shoulder-length wavy dark purple hair, glowing purple eyes, black cropped jacket with purple stitching over a tight purple tank top, black tactical pants with purple side stripes, black fingerless gloves, purple-black sneakers, and the silver grapnel cane with purple wrapping (both extended and collapsed forms). The purple media visor is part of her design.\n<Subject 2> is <Picture 2> Jaro Venn from the second character reference sheet: slick black hair with precise side part, strong defined jawline, warm tan skin, confident expression, brown eyes, iridescent shiny purple high-collar suit with structured shoulders and long coat tails, silver metallic vertical strips on the lapels and vest, white dress shirt, and black gloves. His signature prop is the set of blank white key-cards with thin purple edges.\n<Subject 3> is <Picture 3> the Crownwell city environment taken from the establishing reference images: the massive central circular cyan energy vortex, towering white-and-purple skyscrapers, elevated walkways, neon signage, reflective metallic surfaces, and the overall high-tech plaza layout under mixed daylight and neon lighting.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] A 5-second high-energy action sequence in Crownwell. <Subject 1> (Pixel Dusk) swings into the central plaza on her grapnel cane, lands, activates her media visor, and engages <Subject 2> (Jaro Venn), who deploys holographic shields from his key-cards. The environment (<Subject 3>) remains consistent throughout. Fast cuts, dynamic camera angles, and strong motion inspired by Riot Worlds cinematic style.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in all shots): fully_preserved - exact appearance, clothing, proportions, hair, eye color, and props from the character sheet are maintained with no redesign.\n<Subject 2> (appears from Shot 4 onward): fully_preserved - exact face, hair, skin tone, suit design, silver accents, and key-card prop from the character sheet are maintained with no redesign.\n<Subject 3> (background in all shots): fully_preserved - the central cyan vortex, architecture, color palette, and plaza layout from the establishing references are kept consistent.\n\ndetailed_description:\n[Shot 1] High-detail 2D digital illustration matching the clean cel-shaded style of the character reference sheets. Extreme wide high-angle shot of Crownwell (<Subject 3>) with the glowing cyan energy vortex at the center of the plaza. <Subject 1> swings in on the fully extended grapnel cane from a high building, body arched, purple energy trailing along the cable.\n[Shot 2] At 00:00.800, the camera cuts to a dynamic low-angle medium tracking shot on a reflective metallic walkway. <Subject 1> lands hard, knees bent, the grapnel cane collapsing into its short baton form while the purple media visor flips down over her eyes with a bright glow. She holds a ready, forward-leaning stance.\n[Shot 3] At 00:01.600, the camera cuts to an extreme close-up of <Subject 1>’s face. The media visor is fully engaged, glowing purple lenses framing her intense purple eyes. Soft hair movement and neon reflections slide across the visor surface.\n[Shot 4] At 00:02.400, the camera cuts to a medium 3/4 view of <Subject 2> standing in the plaza with the cyan vortex visible behind him. He turns sharply, raising a fan of blank key-cards that begin emitting soft holographic purple light.\n[Shot 5] At 00:03.200, the camera cuts to a fast side-angle tracking shot of the confrontation. <Subject 1> swings the re-extended grapnel cane in a powerful arc with purple energy trails and motion blur. <Subject 2> raises the key-cards, which expand into large translucent holographic purple geometric shields.\n[Shot 6] At 00:04.100, the camera cuts to a high-angle Dutch-tilt impact frame. The tip of the grapnel cane collides with the holographic shields in a bright purple-cyan energy explosion with sparks and particles. Both characters recoil slightly while the Crownwell vortex pulses brighter in the background.\n\noverall_soundscape: Distant city hum mixed with the low-frequency energy drone of the central vortex. Metallic whoosh and cable snap of the grapnel, hard boot impact on metal plating, soft fabric movement, rising holographic energy crackle, and a sharp high-frequency clash at the final impact.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: Fast-tempo electronic track with driving distorted bass, sharp synth stabs locked to the cuts, rising filtered noise risers into the clash, and a short aggressive low-end punch on the final impact before a quick cutoff.",
